  "listen": "Good morning. This is The Daily Brief for Monday, October 12, 2026. The lead story is about Russia and Ukraine. President Trump said he had brokered a cease-fire to protect energy infrastructure in both countries. Ukrainian officials say bombs kept falling overnight on gas facilities, wounding 33 people. Ukraine's leader says Russia is ignoring the energy ceasefire. Moscow has said little about the proposal. Now the front page. Saudi Arabia's minister vowed a serious response after Houthi attacks hit Riyadh's international airport and another facility, killing 13 people. Federal agents searched the Washington home of Representative Ilhan Omar. The Justice Department says the warrant was approved as part of an ongoing federal investigation. Omar calls it an attempt to target political enemies. In France, a fourteen-year-old was detained after two teachers were shot at a middle school. And Drop Site News reports on Iran tightening control of the Strait of Hormuz. Now, a sentence for each section. In Tech and AI, Cloudflare is acquiring Deno outright. In Politics, the Justice Department is investigating TV networks for possible antitrust violations. In World, a seafarers' union official says crews are being offered big money to transit the Strait of Hormuz. In Sports, the 49ers say Deebo Samuel will miss at least a couple of weeks with a hamstring injury. In Atlanta, one person died and four were injured on the Goliath rollercoaster at Six Flags Over Georgia. The Atlanta Dream reached the WNBA Finals. In Architecture, Hexagon will acquire Rocscience for 535 million dollars. In Science and Nature, Chinook salmon are returning to the Klamath River after four US dams were removed. That is the brief. Have a good day.",
